WEBVTT

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:06.560
What happened to that case?

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:09.780
It was treated as trouble
occurring between Dead Apostles.

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:13.820
No penalties for us nor for Policies.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:16.450
I see.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:19.450
So, you heard about my big sister?

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:21.790
Um, uh, well...

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:23.330
I'm sorry.

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:25.670
Oh no, it's fine!

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:28.380
I've told Flat and the others long ago.

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:31.380
Is that so?

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:37.850
My big sister had
a lot more talent than I do.

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:40.890
There are times when I think,
"What if she had met Sir?"

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:43.890
But I like it here.

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:49.570
I'm glad I was able to come here,

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:52.820
and that I was able to meet everyone.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:55.650
Me, too.

00:00:56.490 --> 00:00:59.370
Everyone is waiting
for you and Sir to return.

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:03.950
When Svin heard that you got injured,
he had such a look on his face!

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:05.790
Such a look?

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:09.250
So maybe he does detest me.

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:13.130
Is Gray-tan all right? Gray-tan...

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:19.390
I want to suck in Gray-tan's sweet, beautiful
and slightly melancholy scent now if I could!

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:24.060
That's why you get banned
from her room, Le Chien!

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:27.020
Don't call me Le Chien!
To begin with, because you—

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:29.560
If you're gonna make a scene, leave!
Both of you!

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:32.360
Especially Svin!
You should know your place!

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:34.530
I-I'm sorry, sir!

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:38.450
Oh, that's right!

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:40.120
Here you go, Professor!

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:42.280
What is this?

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:45.580
What? It's a book
you'd be delighted to see!

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.500
A book that guys just love!

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:48.500
That's right!

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:50.170
EXCITING LOVE
Official Game Guide

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:50.170
A strategy guide for Gal-ge!

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:54.050
Professor, I heard you were
a passionate researcher of Japanese games!

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:56.050
Let me assist you!

00:01:58.510 --> 00:02:01.220
Whoa, looks like things are heating up!

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:03.560
I can't overlook this as a spy!

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:06.770
Weren't you being detained by Policies?

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:10.100
I made a plea bargain,
so they released me!

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:12.270
Anyways,

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:15.530
someone real, compared to a game...

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:19.990
I don't care! All of you, get out! What would
normally heal won't heal with you around!

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:22.410
Jeez.

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:26.620
If they didn't make such a ruckus,
I would've been discharged a lot sooner.

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:30.540
Aren't they all just eager
to have you back, sir?

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:35.800
It's all thanks to Father Karabo
that we both made it back alive.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:38.800
Yes.

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:41.300
He saved us until the very end.

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:45.010
But I was not able to save him.

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:47.520
Sir...

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:53.730
Congratulations on your recovery.

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:55.940
I appreciate you coming out to say that.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:03:00.950
The case from seven years ago
will go unmentioned after all.

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:02.950
I see.

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:06.950
The Holy Church didn't seem to want it
brought back into the limelight after all this time.

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:12.710
There was one thing I wanted to ask you.

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:14.710
What is it?

00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:18.420
You must surely be aware of the holes
in your own deduction?

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:21.340
The reason why he summoned
a Servant, is it?

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:24.600
It is true that Ghost Liners
are precious resources.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:28.220
I can understand how one would go
so far to summon one.

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:32.140
If it's simply a matter of rarity,
a Jewel-class Mystic Eyes will do.

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:35.020
Why does it have to be a Heroic Spirit?

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:37.900
What do you think about that?

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:41.490
I'm sure there is more to this case.

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:47.120
He said he'd be troubled
if I died right now.

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:49.580
It's all about being necessities
for the future.

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:51.370
Both myself and that Faker.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:53.000
Yes.

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:56.460
In due time, I'll face that man once again.

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:58.210
I'm sure of it.

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:03.470
<i>Overturn thyself!</i>

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.020
I wanted to ask you a question, too.

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:11.350
Go ahead.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:14.020
Trisha's pendant...

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:16.900
Why did you leave it behind?

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:21.990
I'm sure you have some sort
of hypothesis about that, as well.

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:25.030
You said you were on that train
on personal business.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:30.240
Taking such drastic actions, confusing
the crowd with a mistaken deduction...

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:32.790
Wasn't there someone
you wanted to lure out?

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:36.630
Are you saying
everything was what I'd intended?

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:38.290
So, it wasn't?

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:41.050
You're overestimating me.

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:46.590
Of course, the motive is as you've deduced.

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:49.430
After all, I did assist you, didn't I?

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:51.720
Yeah. Without your assistance,

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:54.310
I wouldn't have been able
to restrain that fake Caules.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.310
I saved your life.

00:04:56.310 --> 00:04:57.400
In hindsight!

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:00.900
The answer to your question...

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:04.490
is something similar to you and Ms. Reines.

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:10.200
Doctor Heartless is my elder brother-in-law.

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:14.160
Both of us were adopted children of Norwich.

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:17.000
I see.

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:19.460
By the way, I have
one more question to ask.

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:21.840
Something else?

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:26.470
Why did you give up on bidding
and drop out in the final phase?

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:29.220
If Reines took five more minutes
to arrive, I...

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:30.510
Oh my.

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:34.480
Were you trusting Policies by chance?

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:54.830
Oh? Elder Brother and Gray
have just been discharged.

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:01.340
Do people say you unfortunately
miss out on things?

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:05.380
It's not like I came here
to see the two of them!

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:07.630
Pardon me, then.

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:11.600
I heard you helped out
with treatment on my elder brother.

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:14.720
I couldn't afford Animusphere
to owe a favor.

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:16.270
I see.

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:20.020
I do appreciate what he did about Trisha.

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:23.270
Lord El-Melloi spoke her words
on her behalf.

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:27.820
If this was my elder brother,
he'd say, "Please add the suffix II."

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:30.870
Father...

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:33.160
would not even see me.

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:34.410
Oh?

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:37.080
If The Greater Grail met Father's...

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:40.330
Maris Billy's expectations,

00:06:41.210 --> 00:06:43.960
I'm sure his dream would've been realized.

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:48.720
But that is a time and a world
unbeknownst to me.

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:52.260
I didn't expect you to be such the poet.

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:54.970
I like you.

00:06:55.220 --> 00:06:58.350
In other words, you want
a fair exchange of information, right?

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:02.270
We are both in line
to succeed the title of Lord.

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:09.030
I don't think it's a bad thing to use
this opportunity to deepen our relations.

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:12.990
You are quite different
from that elder brother of yours.

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:16.290
Well, of course.
We're not related by blood after all.

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:20.960
I see. I think I can be
good friends with you.

00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:26.500
Nice to be of acquaintance
as long as we can be of utility for one another.

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:50.530
Mr. Melvin?

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:07.130
There was a special
stockholders' meeting at Mom's hotel.

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:08.960
It was a huge mess.

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:11.130
You seem to be busy.

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:14.430
Mages do have lives, after all.

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:18.350
So, um...

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:23.440
I tune the damaged main Crest
of the El-Melloi faction.

00:08:24.140 --> 00:08:26.810
But separate from that,
I'm also in possession...

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:30.900
of Waver's Magical Crest
for the Velvet Family.

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:35.200
Magical Crest! The thing Mages inherit
from one generation to another!

00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:36.700
Right.

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:40.200
What you could say
is the biggest family heirloom.

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:43.660
Why do you have it, Mr. Melvin?

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:48.630
You know how Waver shouldered all
of El-Melloi's debt from Lady Reines, right?

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:52.260
What he used as collateral for it
was his Magical Crest.

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:56.470
If someone was holding it for him,
I'd be the natural choice as a Tuner, right?

00:08:57.140 --> 00:08:58.260
So, Sir...

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:01.100
took something that important to him...

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:07.350
It's the best collateral to collect
in terms of not making a Mage betray you!

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:10.610
I mean, it's synonymous as taking
their purpose in life away from them.

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:16.160
Their purpose in life...

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:23.950
Um, I've been curious for a while.

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:29.380
Why do you call him "Waver," Mr. Melvin?

00:09:31.550 --> 00:09:34.260
Because it'd be lonely
if nobody called him Waver

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:37.640
when he relinquishes the title of Lord.

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:39.390
Lonely?

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:44.520
It may be true that the Holy Grail War
affected Waver greatly.

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:46.350
But...

00:09:46.690 --> 00:09:51.480
the 19 years leading up to that
must've been valuable for him, as well.

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:56.490
That, and the time after he stops being a Lord,
which will arrive at some point.

00:09:56.490 --> 00:09:59.410
When he is no longer a Lord?

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:04.870
You look like you've never thought about it.

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:12.920
He's been changing until now,
triggered by trivial things, hasn't he?

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:15.550
I'm sure he'll continue to do so.

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:18.760
For instance, something
like the Fifth Holy Grail War.

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:24.430
And if that happens, he may perhaps
depart from this place for good.

00:10:27.850 --> 00:10:29.690
Even if that were to happen,

00:10:30.560 --> 00:10:31.810
for me,

00:10:32.060 --> 00:10:33.900
Sir will still be Sir.

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:36.190
He will be for everyone in the class, as well.

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:40.660
Yeah. I think that's fine in its own way.

00:10:41.030 --> 00:10:43.700
Various people have
varying sides to them.

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:46.080
It was fun to chat with you.

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:48.160
Well, I'll be going now.

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:02.970
Lord El-Melloi II's Case Files
｛Rail Zeppelin｝Grace note

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:11.690
Wandering child adrift in darkness,

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:12.980
step forward!

00:11:16.190 --> 00:11:20.400
Answer with thy name establishing thee
within this transient world.

00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:23.160
My name is Svin Glascheit.

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:26.620
I seek to reach the Root
using the wisdom of the beasts.

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:29.500
Thou art a child of the stars.

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:36.380
In this moment, thou art born of darkness
and given life within the light.

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:50.060
On my name as Lord El-Melloi,

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:53.730
I grant thee, Svin Glascheit,
the rank of Pride.

00:11:57.320 --> 00:12:00.990
Another one of my students
has surpassed me.

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:05.530
I'm confident in how to use my feet.

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:11.210
I've come this far all thanks to you, sir.

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:14.540
Me and probably Flat, too.

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:18.800
It's thanks to being taught
by none other than you.

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:23.300
With this, we will conclude the ritual.

00:12:23.550 --> 00:12:29.010
All witnesses, please greet with great applause
our blessed child seeking the Root!

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:42.780
And yet another one of his students rise
to the third rank of the Clock Tower.

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:49.790
Goodness gracious, your performance
is a bit scary, Lord El-Melloi II.

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:53.790
Man, you really are amazing, Svin!

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:56.250
I'll never forget about you, genius!

00:12:57.420 --> 00:12:59.710
Man, it's not like
I'm graduating or anything.

00:13:01.260 --> 00:13:06.050
You're just getting all set to fall from
a child prodigy to a normal person at age 20!

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:08.760
You're not complimenting me
at all, are you?

00:13:12.140 --> 00:13:14.810
You're not thundering
down on them like usual.

00:13:14.810 --> 00:13:18.060
You're in a surprisingly good mood,
Elder Brother.

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:19.150
Yeah.

00:13:19.400 --> 00:13:22.150
I finally feel like a burden
has been lifted from my shoulders.

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:25.860
I'm troubled if you sound like an old man

00:13:25.860 --> 00:13:28.660
just because you have
one more student with a Pride rank.

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:31.240
As my tutor, you need to—

00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:32.450
That's right!

00:13:32.450 --> 00:13:36.370
I must continue to get up close
and intimate with who I am spying on!

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:38.080
You know...

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:42.340
<i>He may perhaps depart
from this place for good.</i>

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:45.300
<i>Sir!</i>

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:48.470
<i>It can't be!</i>

00:13:57.900 --> 00:14:00.480
Perhaps, you're drinking a bit too much.

00:14:00.810 --> 00:14:05.950
Lady, I may be a cheap drunk,
but this much won't affect me.

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:11.990
In the first place, Reines was drinking
ten times as much during that party earlier.

00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:16.830
I feel Ms. Reines holds her drink
a bit too well.

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:19.500
It will affect your performance tomorrow!

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:24.800
The party was very lively.

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:30.510
Yeah. It's not often that you see someone
rise to Pride while in their teens.

00:14:31.390 --> 00:14:32.810
Just like my predecessor.

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:37.520
With that, my predecessor,

00:14:38.190 --> 00:14:42.860
Kayneth El-Melloi Archibald,
was established as a child prodigy.

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:48.150
And pushing all other factions aside,
he reigned as a great Lord.

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:53.740
That was likely
because everyone had to admit...

00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:59.580
the scenery that he'd been seeing
was ideal for Mages.

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:05.050
It's a scenery that I couldn't share
to the end. Not once.

00:15:10.010 --> 00:15:13.300
I'm on the side of simply celebrating

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:15.930
and sending out my students as usual.

00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:16.770
Um...

00:15:18.890 --> 00:15:22.650
I have been saved thanks to you!

00:15:23.270 --> 00:15:27.110
Because you've brought me out of that village!

00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:34.490
I'm sure everyone appreciates you
for all sorts of reasons.

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:36.080
So...

00:15:36.950 --> 00:15:38.080
So...

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:42.830
Svin told me the same thing earlier.

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:52.340
Perpetually a half-assed Lord incapable
of doing anything like his great predecessor...

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:56.350
I still think that way about myself.

00:15:57.100 --> 00:15:59.600
But if all of you guys tell me what you do,

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:01.850
maybe just a little bit...

00:16:04.810 --> 00:16:05.650
Sir,

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:07.780
will you be heading out after all?

00:16:09.610 --> 00:16:11.740
About the Fifth Holy Grail War...

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:14.450
I officially...

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:17.120
stepped down from contention.

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:19.040
Why?

00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:23.710
Participating in a Holy Grail War
is settling matters for me personally.

00:16:24.040 --> 00:16:26.290
It isn't settling matters
for the Heroic Spirit Iskandar.

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:28.920
I have my regrets,

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:30.800
but it's nothing to be so fixated over.

00:16:31.840 --> 00:16:33.340
As one of his subjects

00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:36.050
and as a Lord of the Clock Tower,

00:16:36.800 --> 00:16:41.810
the battlefield where I need to bring things
to an end is not over there!

00:16:42.350 --> 00:16:46.940
I'll dismantle the ploy he's trying
to achieve by using Faker's,

00:16:47.190 --> 00:16:50.690
in other words Iskandar's, power!

00:16:52.820 --> 00:16:55.360
That, in fact, is what my duty is.

00:16:56.070 --> 00:16:57.490
Sir...

00:16:58.370 --> 00:17:00.830
Gray, can you stand aside?

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:02.620
Sure!

00:17:03.160 --> 00:17:05.120
I'm going to get some fresh air.

00:17:05.120 --> 00:17:06.130
Um,

00:17:06.580 --> 00:17:07.380
this...

00:17:07.380 --> 00:17:09.750
I got it at the department store
with Ms. Reines and company...

00:17:11.920 --> 00:17:15.970
Actually, I was thinking
about giving this to you sooner!

00:17:19.890 --> 00:17:21.140
I'm sorry!

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:23.020
I'm sure accepting
something like this isn't...

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:26.310
Am I not always telling you, Lady?

00:17:27.020 --> 00:17:28.520
The whydunit.

00:17:29.190 --> 00:17:30.320
What is important...

00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:33.610
is why you went through with it.

00:17:38.070 --> 00:17:39.070
Gray,

00:17:39.330 --> 00:17:43.450
I'm sorry, but I'm sure
my powers won't be enough.

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:45.830
I want you to fight together with me.

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:48.830
If you are...

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:51.420
fine with me.

00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:53.760
Thank you.

00:17:54.380 --> 00:17:57.180
And I'm counting on you in the future.

00:18:00.890 --> 00:18:03.470
Snow... It's early this year.

00:18:03.850 --> 00:18:05.480
You know, Le Chien?

00:18:05.480 --> 00:18:10.400
They say that when it snows in Japan,
dogs run around on the bottom right of your screen.

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:12.820
I'm sure you're mixing two things
in that statement.

00:18:13.070 --> 00:18:16.950
This is new. You're not quipping
with the usual "Don't call me a dog"?

00:18:16.950 --> 00:18:20.870
Well, I was told to stay calm
to suit my rank of Pride.

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:22.950
Oh, you've matured!

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:26.410
But that's not just me, is it?

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:29.540
Yeah. Everyone has learned from him.

00:18:31.710 --> 00:18:32.840
Oh, it's Gray!

00:18:33.800 --> 00:18:36.550
Where, where, where? Where's Gray-tan?

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:40.430
And what happened to staying calm
to suit your rank of Pride?

00:18:44.010 --> 00:18:44.890
Yes.

00:18:46.430 --> 00:18:48.060
Finally,

00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:51.150
one of my students...

00:18:51.560 --> 00:18:52.730
is headed that way.

00:19:11.420 --> 00:19:13.420
You can assault him
as much as you want now!

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:16.380
Why don't you go ahead
and take his lips now or something?

00:19:42.320 --> 00:19:44.160
What's wrong, boy?

00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:46.160
You coming over here?

00:19:48.870 --> 00:19:51.040
This is just a dream.

00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:55.670
Merely an illusion that my brain
and my memories have created.

00:19:57.550 --> 00:20:02.550
What's this? You've gotten to wringing out
words in some logical manner?

00:20:02.970 --> 00:20:04.260
Of course.

00:20:04.600 --> 00:20:06.680
It's what I lecture all the time.

00:20:08.020 --> 00:20:10.560
But to think you'd be a teacher...

00:20:11.310 --> 00:20:13.690
Complete with creases
between your brows.

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:18.230
Even if the Holy Grail War is over,
life continues...

00:20:18.820 --> 00:20:20.900
to the point of absurdity.

00:20:23.070 --> 00:20:26.700
Perhaps, I've changed a bit since then.

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:30.580
Maybe I haven't changed at all.

00:20:31.250 --> 00:20:33.040
The one thing I can say, though,

00:20:33.790 --> 00:20:38.460
is that I still can't stand alongside you yet!

00:20:41.300 --> 00:20:47.180
Because the pain of the path leading there
and the glory at its end

00:20:47.810 --> 00:20:50.140
must be gained in real life.

00:20:51.020 --> 00:20:52.350
Not here,

00:20:52.770 --> 00:20:53.810
but in my...

00:20:54.310 --> 00:20:56.860
in the battlefield of Lord El-Melloi II!

00:20:57.440 --> 00:20:58.480
I see.

00:20:59.360 --> 00:21:03.700
Then, I, as a transient dream,
shall dare to ask this...

00:21:07.780 --> 00:21:11.120
Has your journey so far been fun for you?

00:21:12.450 --> 00:21:13.410
Yeah.

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:16.830
Of course...

00:21:18.540 --> 00:21:19.800
Rider.

00:21:21.800 --> 00:21:23.380
This is a journey...

00:21:24.180 --> 00:21:25.840
to follow in your legacy!

00:22:06.470 --> 00:22:09.970
Lord El-Melloi II's Case Files
｛Rail Zeppelin｝ Grace note

00:22:07.840 --> 00:22:09.970
We're starting class now!
